<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Batch</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="99.56%" size="4" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Mesh &gt; Batch</b></span></i> <span lang="EN-GB">or by pressing</span> <b><span class="Shortcut" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Ctrl + H</b></span></b><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span></b> <span class="Command">Batch</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command carries out a series of mesh functions automatically.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><img src="../images/image1.jpg" width="479px" height="367px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Fill holes up to</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Fills holes with less than the given number of edges. Default value is up to 50 edges.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Remove floating meshes up to</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Removes regions, which are isolated from the main mesh. Default value is up to 500 triangles.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Decimate triangles with thinnest angle of less than</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Removes triangles that have angle less than the given degree. This stage produces the same results as if you call</span> <u style="text-decoration:none;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="text-decoration:none;">Select Thin Triangles</span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">command and then delete the selection. Default value is less than 10 degrees.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB">Remove triangles forming 3D angles of less than</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Removes triangles, which planes form 3D angle less than the given degree. Default value is less than 60 degrees.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Reduce noise</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Reduces noise by replacing each point with the average of its neighbour points. Default value is minimum strength.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Group Polygon count reduction</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Reduces the number of polygons while trying to preserve the quality of the mesh.</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="margin-left:19px;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>3D tolerance</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB"> decimation removes vertices from areas with less detail than the rest of the selected data set. This option decimates the data using the given number. Default value is = 0.01mm.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="margin-left:19px;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Optimising</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB"> decimation algorithms are optimising either speed or accuracy. For example, if the slider is on maximum accuracy you will be running the 'preserving features' decimation only, which is rather slow. Default value is 'Optimize by accuracy'.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="margin-left:19px;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Keep triangles with edges less than</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB"> after reduction all triangles will have with edges equal or less than the value set. This is useful if the features quality is important. Default value is do not restrict triangles edge length.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="margin-left:19px;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Sort triangles</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB"> reorganises the redraw sequence of triangles. Default value is sort triangles.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is grayed if there is no selection or all selections are hidden. It works on wholly selected entities as well as on partial selections.</span></p>
